    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0935" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.48A6 Liquor/11: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Capetown</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                        Courcy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Capetown</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-07-20T15:00:00+02:00">July 20, 1936—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 20—10:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s telegram of July 18, noon, full report on this
                    situation being submitted airmail today.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d676-f1"/> Wine
                    Grower’s Association is conducting violent propaganda campaign against American
                    goods following closing American office. Campaign, though not justified by
                    facts, is obtaining support from deciduous fruit growers and is having harmful
                    effect American trade. It would be very helpful if Department could ascertain
                    from Department of <pb facs="0936" n="856" xml:id="pg856"/> Agriculture and
                    cable if any revision of BPQ 362<anchor n="2" xml:id="d676-f2"/> along the lines
                    suggested by South African entomologists who were in Washington last October is
                    contemplated. Must discuss situation with Decidious Fruit Exchange Thursday.</p>
                <p>I have no knowledge wine shipments held up here account regulation. Have
                    consistently sent Association copies all liquor regulation[s] received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">De Courcy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
